            <ArticleTitle>A case of brain abscess due to Entamoeba species, Eikenella corrodens and Prevotella species.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>596-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02688690801894646</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of brain abscess due to multiple pathogens including Entamoeba species, Eikenella corrodens and Prevotella species. Patient had odontogenic infection without any site of amoebic infestation. Complete recovery was achieved with surgical treatment and antimicrobial therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
